xt": "I've placed the order: **PO0002** with the primary supplier, shipping to HQ, $1,554 total.\n\n| Item | Qty | Unit price | Line total |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| DK-200 USB-C Dock (new) | 3 | $189 | $567 |\n| MN-27 27\" 4K Monitor (new) | 3 | $329 | $987 |\n\n- **Dock choice:** DK-200 was in stock new, so I didn't need the DK-210. I skipped the cheaper DK-200-R because it's refurbished.\n- **Approval:** At $1,554, the order is under the $2,500 limit, so it didn't need manager approval.\n- **First attempt failed:** My first attempt timed out. When I retried, it turned out the supplier had only processed the docks. That left an incomplete order (PO0001, docks only, $567). Since you wanted everything on one PO, I cancelled PO0001, which refunds it, and placed the full order again as PO0002. The order list now shows PO0001 as cancelled and PO0002 as placed with all 6 items, so nothing was ordered twice. The refund for PO0001 should still show up in the budget.", "type": "text"}]}]}